\end{array}$$

$\quad \frac{1}{2} \mathrm{l} \omega^{2}+\frac{1}{2} \mathrm{~m} \mathrm{v}^{2}=\mathrm{mgh}$
$$\begin{array}{l}
\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{m R^{2}}{2}\right)\left(\frac{v^{2}}{R^{2}}\right)+\frac{1}{2} m v^{2}=m g h \\
\frac{3 v^{2}}{4}=g h \\
h=\frac{3 v^{2}}{4 g}
\end{array}$$

